// @check
// @error not all code paths return a value in 'k'
// CONTRACT (must-error): a body ending in a bare `{ … }` has NO implicit return. D1901
// ruled the bare block a statement, `drwBareBlock` lowers it to an else-less `if true`, and
// the emitter's tail ladder drops that value and pads the fall-through with `unreachable` —
// padding it calls sound "because the typechecker proved that path dead". The totality rule
// used to prove exactly that, so this program checked clean and trapped (D1902). The
// un-annotated spelling of the same body is `void`, and the `if true { 5 }` it lowers to is
// refused with this sentence, so the annotated spelling owes it too.
function k(): i32 {
  {
    5
  }
}
print(k())
